AWS S3 Bucket Backup and Cleanup via Terraform
Overview
This task involves automating the cleanup of an obsolete AWS S3 bucket (devops-bck-141920337) using Terraform and the AWS CLI. The operation ensures that the bucket's contents are safely backed up locally to the /opt/s3-backup/ directory on the infrastructure node before the bucket and its objects are completely removed.

Task Requirements
Copy the contents of the devops-bck-141920337 S3 bucket to /opt/s3-backup/ on the target host.

Delete the S3 bucket (devops-bck-141920337).

Implement the solution using a Terraform null_resource and local-exec provisioner inside /home/bob/terraform/main.tf.

Implementation (main.tf)
Terraform
resource "null_resource" "s3_cleanup" {
  provisioner "local-exec" {
    command = <<EOT
      mkdir -p /opt/s3-backup/
      aws s3 cp s3://devops-bck-141920337/ /opt/s3-backup/ --recursive
      aws s3 rb s3://devops-bck-141920337/ --force
    EOT
  }
}
Execution Steps
Navigate to the Terraform working directory:

Bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
Initialize the Terraform providers and modules:

Bash
terraform init
Apply the Terraform configuration to execute the backup and cleanup routine:

Bash
terraform apply -auto-approve
Verification
Verify local backup contents:

Bash
ls -la /opt/s3-backup/
Expected output: Confirms downloaded files (e.g., devops.txt) are present in the target directory.

Verify S3 bucket deletion:

Bash
aws s3 ls
